1
00:00:08,359 --> 00:00:09,160
Fu Ting.

2
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:12,800
Your death sentence will now be carried out.

3
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,199
Do you have any last words?

4
00:00:17,359 --> 00:00:19,000
It wasn't me.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,239
It wasn't me!

6
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,679
Your son wanted me to ask you,

7
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:30,120
do you regret killing him?

8
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:34,920
I don't regret it.

9
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,000
They all deserved to die.

10
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:41,159
They all deserved to die!

11
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,920
I really couldn't take it anymore.

12
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,120
Five years.

13
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,280
They never treated me like a human being.

14
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,120
From inside the room, I saw

15
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,479
that axe.

16
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:16,120
I just kept hacking away,

17
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,840
fueled by alcohol, venting

18
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,120
everything pent up over the years.

19
00:02:21,879 --> 00:02:23,319
Since you studied law,

20
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,639
let's not beat around the bush.

21
00:02:25,319 --> 00:02:27,319
You know what dismemberment means.

22
00:02:28,639 --> 00:02:30,039
The scene where we found the body parts

23
00:02:30,039 --> 00:02:31,520
was at a construction site out east.

24
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,759
Two construction workers,

25
00:02:34,159 --> 00:02:35,120
on their way home,

26
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,520
saw a pack of dogs digging in the dirt.

27
00:02:36,719 --> 00:02:38,080
They walked over to look,

28
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,199
and found these human remains.

29
00:02:41,479 --> 00:02:42,400
The deceased was confirmed

30
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,319
to be a middle-aged woman in her fifties.

31
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:47,360
Don't move! Don't move!

32
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,919
Let go of me! Let me go!

33
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,280
You liar!

34
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,879
You dirty liar!

35
00:02:53,319 --> 00:02:55,439
Let me go! Let me go!

36
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,319
Let go of me!

37
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,719
Let me go! Let go of me!

38
00:03:15,719 --> 00:03:17,120
I really like you.

39
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,199
I'll screw you first,

40
00:03:18,439 --> 00:03:19,680
and then kill you.

41
00:03:20,319 --> 00:03:21,919
The 50,000-yuan bride price

42
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,840
also went down the drain.

43
00:03:24,439 --> 00:03:26,319
I went to their family for compensation,

44
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:28,319
but his daughter wouldn't acknowledge it.

45
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:31,240
I prepared six kilograms of sodium cyanide.

46
00:03:31,439 --> 00:03:32,599
I took that packet of poison...

47
00:03:33,159 --> 00:03:35,280
I dumped the whole packet into their well.

48
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:47,879
Bro!

49
00:03:47,879 --> 00:03:48,360
Bro!

50
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,919
I'll strangle you!

51
00:03:48,919 --> 00:03:49,879
Bro, bro, bro!

52
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:51,319
Bro!

53
00:03:53,319 --> 00:03:53,759
Bro!

54
00:03:54,319 --> 00:03:55,120
Get off me!

55
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:59,199
Your dad had just finished a cigarette,

56
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:01,240
sitting on the couch yelling at you.

57
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:04,319
You took a hammer to the back of his head.

58
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:06,879
He didn't even have time to fight back.

59
00:04:06,919 --> 00:04:08,240
Your mom tried to run,

60
00:04:08,719 --> 00:04:11,439
but you struck her down blow after blow.

61
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,000
Drop the knife!

62
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,759
Stay back!

63
00:04:14,759 --> 00:04:15,280
Put it down!

64
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,199
Come any closer and I'll kill her!

65
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:17,240
Give me the child!

66
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:18,759
All right.

67
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,720
Quick, go bring her over.

68
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,319
Brother Baokui, Brother Baokui!

69
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:25,879
What is it?

70
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,120
My wife...

71
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:34,800
That's my wife!

72
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,879
Back off! Back off!

73
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:36,399
Fine, I'm backing off.

74
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:37,000
Step back!

75
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:37,639
I'm stepping back.

76
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,720
I want a car.

77
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,560
Hold on.

78
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,600
Give me the radio.

79
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:44,720
Get a car ready.

80
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,600
Get a car ready!

81
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:54,040
If there's an afterlife,

82
00:04:54,319 --> 00:04:56,240
I hope I'll find happiness.

83
00:05:05,279 --> 00:05:07,279
Even if I had to die ten more times,

84
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,399
I'd still kill you.

85
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:12,319
Next life, we will live well together.

86
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,879
In this life,

87
00:05:16,639 --> 00:05:18,639
this is the only thing I can do for you.

88
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,079
Number 14, Fu Ting.

89
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:33,959
You're up. You're the last one.

90
00:05:49,319 --> 00:05:50,120
The last one.

91
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,600
Yes, Attorney Yan.

92
00:05:54,519 --> 00:05:55,319
Fu Ting.

93
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:57,319
I know who you are.

94
00:05:58,079 --> 00:05:59,079
My firm isn't the right fit for you.

95
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,199
You may leave.

96
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:01,439
Attorney Yan.

97
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,279
I graduated with a J.D. from the

98
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:04,639
University of California, Los Angeles.

99
00:06:05,319 --> 00:06:07,319
A key lawyer in the O. J. Simpson case,

100
00:06:07,319 --> 00:06:09,839
I worked at Shapiro's firm for eight years.

101
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,720
I've studied every major American case.

102
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,839
I believe that within this firm of yours,

103
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,959
not many could surpass me.

104
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:19,920
Here with me,

105
00:06:21,199 --> 00:06:22,519
those are all your disadvantages.

106
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:25,839
I'm busy.

107
00:06:27,079 --> 00:06:27,800
You can go now.

108
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,600
Why?

109
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:31,959
On what grounds, Attorney Yan?

110
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:36,240
I saw your speech in LA last year,

111
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,720
which made me return as a criminal lawyer.

112
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:41,439
I hope you can respect my respect for you.

113
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:42,240
Fine, then.

114
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,920
Since you ask so sincerely,

115
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,000
I'll be gracious enough to tell you.

116
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:48,839
Go ahead.

117
00:06:50,839 --> 00:06:52,600
Because you don't understand human nature,

118
00:06:53,399 --> 00:06:54,839
much less this country.

119
00:06:54,959 --> 00:06:55,759
Attorney Yan.

120
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,800
I passed the bar exam a few months ago,

121
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,040
and I got my license.

122
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,160
I've studied countless domestic cases.

123
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,920
I personally believe I'm fully qualified.

124
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,319
Growing up...

125
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:09,079
You were born in a small mountain village.

126
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,839
A miserable family life.

127
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,160
An alcoholic father

128
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,079
beat you and your mom every single day.

129
00:07:18,839 --> 00:07:19,720
You excelled at school.

130
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,240
In high school,

131
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,800
you ranked first in the entire province.

132
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,839
You turned down Tsinghua and Peking,

133
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:26,279
and got admitted to the

134
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,959
University of California, Los Angeles.

135
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:29,279
Your grades were still stellar.

136
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:31,800
Outstanding, even.

137
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,439
You were determined to sever

138
00:07:37,439 --> 00:07:37,920
every single

139
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,759
connection to China,

140
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,199
your memories, and your roots,

141
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:42,240
to become

142
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,839
a Banana—yellow outside, white inside.

143
00:07:45,279 --> 00:07:46,279
I really don't understand.

144
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,839
Why did you come back?

145
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:51,439
Why insist on joining my firm?

146
00:07:53,759 --> 00:07:54,480
Give me a reason.

147
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,399
Mr. Fu,

148
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,319
please see yourself out.

149
00:08:05,519 --> 00:08:06,920
After graduating from college,

150
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,319
I thought that I

151
00:08:12,319 --> 00:08:14,480
had truly become one of them.

152
00:08:14,839 --> 00:08:16,240
Partying with everyone,

153
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,240
working together...

154
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,319
Everything seemed so perfectly harmonious.

155
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,839
And naturally,

156
00:08:24,839 --> 00:08:26,199
I fell in love with a girl.

157
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,000
She was gorgeous.

158
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,360
She looked just like Nastassja Kinski.

159
00:08:32,519 --> 00:08:33,360
You know,

160
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,600
the Nastassja Kinski from the movie,

161
00:08:35,639 --> 00:08:37,200
Paris, Texas.

162
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:39,679
Back then, I thought...

163
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:45,000
Back then, I thought Nastassja Kinski

164
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,559
was the most beautiful girl in the world.

165
00:08:47,519 --> 00:08:48,840
So I started pursuing her.

166
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:54,240
The next morning, I earnestly asked her,

167
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,639
"Does this mean we're dating now?"

168
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,120
She giggled,

169
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,120
for ten minutes.

170
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,840
She just laughed for ten straight minutes.

171
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:11,200
She stared at me like I was a freak,

172
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:13,240
and then she told me,

173
00:09:13,799 --> 00:09:16,120
"Dude, I slept with you

174
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,360
purely out of politeness.

175
00:09:20,559 --> 00:09:21,440
Just politeness."

176
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,759
Attorney Yan, I don't know if you get it,

177
00:09:28,159 --> 00:09:29,440
but at that moment, I realized

178
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,320
that deep down,

179
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,080
in the end,

180
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,039
I would always be an outsider.

181
00:09:35,159 --> 00:09:36,559
All of that so-called harmony,

182
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,120
every single bit of it,

183
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:43,320
was just their hypocritical politeness.

184
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:49,159
Over there, I never received

185
00:09:50,159 --> 00:09:51,519
any genuine acceptance.

186
00:09:51,519 --> 00:09:52,120
None at all.

187
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,960
Not for a single moment.

188
00:09:55,039 --> 00:09:56,240
Do you understand now?

189
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:03,919
Are you sure?

190
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:08,559
Take him to Office 13.

191
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,840
Get all the files ready for him.

192
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,639
Office 13?

193
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:12,840
Yes.

194
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,960
Within one month,

195
00:10:15,559 --> 00:10:17,080
on these 13 cases,

196
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,799
if you can give me

197
00:10:18,799 --> 00:10:21,840
satisfactory analyses and defense plans,

198
00:10:22,639 --> 00:10:23,840
you can stay.

199
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,799
Do you agree?

200
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,399
Attorney Yan, I excel at case analysis.

201
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,919
One month is more than enough.

202
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:37,440
Thank you.

203
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:48,600
These are the cases Attorney Yan requested.

204
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,840
You have full access to them this month.

205
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,639
Someone will arrange your meals every day,

206
00:10:53,639 --> 00:10:55,000
along with fresh clothes.

207
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,039
We'll also monitor you the entire time.

208
00:10:58,799 --> 00:11:01,600
If you find you can't take it anymore,

209
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,720
we will step in.

210
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,840
What? Hold on.

211
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:06,240
I said, if you can't take it,

212
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:06,759
we'll step in.

213
00:11:06,759 --> 00:11:08,000
Who says I can't take it?

214
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:11,840
Good luck.

215
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:12,639
Thanks.

216
00:12:36,759 --> 00:12:38,240
He has nightmares every day.

217
00:12:39,279 --> 00:12:41,879
Yes. Of all the applicants in his batch,

218
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,480
only he held out until the end.

219
00:12:43,799 --> 00:12:46,000
Let's see how long he can hold out.

220
00:12:46,399 --> 00:12:48,759
If he can stick it out

221
00:12:48,799 --> 00:12:51,080
and deliver a report that satisfies us,

222
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,159
he will break free of his id

223
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,559
and confront his true self.

224
00:12:54,879 --> 00:12:57,159
He needs a complete transformation now,

225
00:12:57,159 --> 00:12:58,080
to return to his original purpose.

226
00:13:00,159 --> 00:13:01,240
Where did he come from,

227
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,759
and where will he go?

228
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:08,000
He came from hardship,

229
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,559
just like me.

230
00:13:58,679 --> 00:14:00,200
Where am I?

231
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,279
What are you doing?

232
00:14:07,759 --> 00:14:09,960
What are you doing? Trying to kill me?

233
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,679
You're gonna kill someone!

234
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:17,879
Li Ermiao!

235
00:14:24,519 --> 00:14:25,919
You bastard!

236
00:14:26,799 --> 00:14:28,600
You've gotten pretty bold, haven't you?

237
00:14:28,799 --> 00:14:30,320
Don't think jumping into the river...

238
00:14:30,799 --> 00:14:31,840
...means it's over!

239
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:33,600
It's far from over!

240
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:35,879
What are you doing?

241
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,240
Why are you throwing rocks at me?

242
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:42,799
Haul him up with the net!

243
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,440
You live-in son-in-law!

244
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,399
You might as well just drop dead!

245
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,919
Alive, you're just a waste of space!

246
00:14:52,399 --> 00:14:53,720
Where do you think you're running?

247
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:56,120
Alive, you belong to our family,

248
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,200
and dead, your ghost is ours!

249
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,360
How could this happen?

250
00:15:14,799 --> 00:15:16,120
Hurry, move it over there!

251
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:17,360
Put it down!

252
00:15:18,279 --> 00:15:19,080
This is...

253
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:22,600
Hit him!

254
00:15:23,279 --> 00:15:24,080
Beat him!

255
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:26,399
Don't hit him!

256
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:27,679
You'll kill him!

257
00:15:28,159 --> 00:15:29,320
Stop beating him!

258
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,320
Hit him!

259
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:38,039
Yeah!

260
00:15:38,039 --> 00:15:38,840
Spread him out!

261
00:15:39,399 --> 00:15:40,919
You're committing a crime, you know that?!

262
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,399
Enough!

263
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,000
Why can't they see me?

264
00:15:48,679 --> 00:15:49,559
Hamstring him!

265
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:50,320
Let's see him run now!

266
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,120
Come on, that's enough.

267
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,279
We still have work to do.

268
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:56,919
Consider yourself lucky.

269
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,559
Break it up!
